# Tier-3 Invariant Verification — run 26

**Subject:** `src/NudgeStreamer.sol` @ workspace commit `9611312`
**Purpose:** machine-confirm (or refute) Tier-2's kill of the run's lead candidate.
**Verdict: Leg-B kill is MACHINE-CONFIRMED** — no counterexample under a plain,
well-behaved ERC20 across 452,000+ fuzzed calls on two independent engines, with the
harness demonstrably able to fail (mutation-verified).

## The claim under test

> Per token, `Σ buffer_i <= token.balanceOf(address(streamer))` over every registered
> `(batchMinter, token)` stream, under all sequences of plain-ERC20 operations.

"Plain, well-behaved ERC20" = standard OpenZeppelin `ERC20`, 18 decimals, no
fee-on-transfer, no rebasing, no transfer hooks, no admin clawback, no reentrancy.

## Artifacts (all audit-authored — NEVER report these as project tests)

| Path | Role |
|---|---|
| `workspace/phoenix-nft-staking/test/Invariant_Run26_BufferConservation.t.sol` | Foundry invariant harness + handler, deep deterministic campaign, econ cross-check, mutation tests |
| `workspace/phoenix-nft-staking/test/MedusaTarget_Run26_BufferConservation.sol` | Second-engine (Medusa) target, self-contained, no `forge-std/Test` base |
| `workspace/phoenix-nft-staking/test/patched/MutantNudgeStreamer.sol` | Deliberately broken streamer (1-wei over-credit) used to prove the harness can fail |
| `workspace/phoenix-nft-staking/medusa-run26.json` | Medusa config |

